  {
   "type": "bigtable",
   "title": "17. Interview questions, short answers",
   "cols": [
    "#",
    "Question",
    "Answer"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "VLOOKUP vs XLOOKUP?",
     "XLOOKUP can look left, has a not-found value and is exact by default."
    ],
    [
     "What does $ do in $A$1?",
     "Locks the column and row when you copy."
    ],
    [
     "COUNT vs COUNTA?",
     "COUNT: numbers only. COUNTA: any filled cell."
    ],
    [
     "Remove duplicates?",
     "Data > Remove Duplicates, or UNIQUE in 365."
    ],
    [
     "SUMIF vs SUMIFS?",
     "SUMIF: one condition. SUMIFS: many, sum range first."
    ],
    [
     "What is a pivot table?",
     "A drag-and-drop summary. No formulas needed."
    ],
    [
     "Find duplicates, keep data?",
     "COUNTIF(range, cell)>1 or highlight rules."
    ],
    [
     "What is Flash Fill?",
     "Ctrl + E. Excel repeats the pattern you typed."
    ],
    [
     "Why INDEX + MATCH?",
     "Looks both ways and survives inserted columns."
    ],
    [
     "How do you handle errors?",
     "Fix the cause, then IFERROR or IFNA."
    ],
    [
     "Relative vs absolute?",
     "Relative moves when copied. Absolute stays."
    ],
    [
     "What is data validation?",
     "Rules for what a cell accepts, like a drop-down."
    ],
    [
     "Freeze the header row?",
     "View > Freeze Panes > Freeze Top Row."
    ],
    [
     "What is Power Query for?",
     "Repeatable cleaning: import, clean, combine, refresh."
    ]
   ]
  },
